{
 "about": "Strokes the screen outlines whole (docs/dev/handwriting.md 'Client', 'Server'): a pen stroke without the o channel, neither dashed nor drawn with a calligraphy nib, is frontend/src/ink/ink.js penOutline — perfect-freehand 1.2.2's getStroke with outlineOptions at ten times the page's scale and both ends round (runOutline: perfect-freehand drops the points within 3 units of a path's end, so at the page's own scale the hook case's last 2.5 pt would straighten, and offsets a lone point by 1 unit, so the dot would be an off-centre blob), a two-sample stroke given its midpoint first, then its straight runs cut into quarter-point steps (denseStraights: a segment longer than 0.25 pt next to a sample where the stroke turns by less than 3° and so does a neighbour, or that is next to an end, cut only within 24 steps of each of its ends), so a corner a straight run leads to is not cut by the streamline's lag while a curve keeps its smoothing — and gamma/ink.py draws a pencil or a translucent pen of this kind with pen_outline, the same outline. `d` is ink.js strokePath's path (svgPathFromPoints: a closed path of quadratic curves through the points' midpoints, its numbers as Number.prototype.toFixed(2) writes them); the exporters' numbers are the same to the hundredth.",
